<title>SINGAPORE: Sincere Watch net profit leaps 154 pct.</title>
<headline>Sincere Watch net profit leaps 154 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     1.66  vs   0.65</p>
<p>Dividend (cents)			   0.80  vs   0.45</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    2.54  vs   1.00</p>
<p>    Turnover			     119.04  vs 114.74</p>
<p>Other income incl. interest	    1.74  vs   0.70</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   1.63  vs   1.84</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     1.96  vs   1.18</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.13  vs   0.00</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 4.59  vs   2.19</p>
<p>    Tax					2.20  vs   0.98</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.86  vs   0.56</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: October 17, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open: October 1, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Sincere Watch Ltd said net profit improved as a result of good cost control, aggressive marketing and better margins. The firm expects profit to improve through the current financial year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
